{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P9vFMrN9JCCmEHMxvcKiNp","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:34:$\\lambda_3$ contributes 33.5\\% of conf${\\geq}$2 labels while agreeing 100\\% with 2-LF labels where both are defined; removing it costs 7.7\\,pp (Appendix~\\ref{sec:app_ob_analysis}).\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:126:2-LF (no cmd\\_rep) & 0.6822 & 0.4810 & 0.8840 \\\\\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:135:Removing cmd\\_rep drops macro-F1 by 29.4\\,pp (Table~\\ref{tab:cmd_rep_ablation}; McNemar $p{\\approx}0$) due to data volume collapse: cmd\\_rep expands training data ${\\sim}$10$\\times$ (4K$\\to$43K windows) while agreeing 100\\% with 2-LF labels on overlapping windows---purely a coverage contribution (Appendix~\\ref{sec:app_label_quality}).\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:93:Under the prevalence-matched ablation (\\S\\ref{sec:cmd_rep_ablation}), 3-LF and 2-LF label sets agree on 100\\% of overlapping windows, confirming that cmd\\_rep's contribution is coverage (expanding conf${\\geq}$2 training data from ${\\sim}$4K to ${\\sim}$43K windows) rather than label refinement.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:232:On the 4,070 windows where both 2-LF and 3-LF labels are defined, the two configurations agree on 100\\% of labels: cmd\\_rep does not change any label where the other two LFs already vote.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:234:The 2-LF model's low F1 reflects data volume collapse---too few training examples to learn the stagnation distribution---rather than label corruption.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:338:However, $\\lambda_3$ functions as a coverage expander rather than an independent corrector: across 43,402 windows where both 2-LF and 3-LF configurations produce labels, their agreement is 100\\%."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9kMh3ZhLJdi8fxaMkWqoB","session_id":"5d5323cd-d040-44cc-ba70-9f4e536cb20e","uuid":"104be36f-dcd1-4fde-ac1e-17b668af17af","timestamp":"2026