H windows\n- Larger gold set with higher IAA\n- Third agent or non-SE domain\n- Calibration analysis\n- Window stride/overlap sensitivity\n- Cost-benefit analysis of full pipeline vs direct annotation\n\n**R1's Critical Questions:**\n- Feature overlap ablation shows LF-overlapping features alone exceed full model cross-agent. How is this \"detecting true stagnation\"?\n- Human ceiling given kappa=0.39?\n- Why no probe on full gold set?\n- Nature of the \"version mismatch\" bug?\n- What happens to 97.3% of OH windows where 2-LF abstains?\n","uuid":"e7a102b8-9bff-4bfd-9b5a-f83021ac1b52","session_id":"5d5323cd-d040-44cc-ba70-9f4e536cb20e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) in a roundtable discussion. You previously reviewed this paper focusing on novelty and related work, and gave it a 3/6. Now you have received Reviewer 1's review (focused on methods and experiments). Read R1's review below and provide:\n\n1. Points of agreement with R1\n2. Points of disagreement with R1\n3. Any adjustment to your score (with justification)\n4. Key issues that should appear in the final consolidated review\n\nKeep your response concise (under 400 words).\n\n## R1's Review Summary\n\n**Score: 3/6 (Weak Reject), Soundness 2/4**\n\n**Key Strengths R1 identified:**\n- Honest circularity disclosure\n- Comprehensive ablation design\n- Statistical reporting above average (paired bootstrap, McNemar, instance isolation)\n- Useful negative finding on TLMs\n- Practical framing (cost, latency)\n- LF temporal dynamics analysis (cmd_rep reversal across agents)\n\n**Key Weaknesses R1 identified:**\n- W1: Circularity more severe than acknowledged — LF-overlapping features alone get 0.977 cross-agent; residual features collapse to 0.566. Cross-agent \"transfer\" is largely LF reconstruction on new agent.\n- W2: Gold set underpowered — kappa=0.39, N=52 for 3-annotator IAA, N=505 total. Probe not evaluated on full gold set including OH.\n- W3: Matched-scope comparison conflates evaluation conditions — headline +37.2pp compares different N values (150K vs 6K).\n- W4: Deployment analysis experiments appear incomplete — compute_waste_audit.json shows OH data=0; pareto_curve.py has generate_mock_data() function.\n- W5: Only two agents from same domain on same benchmark.\n- W6: 2-LF \"deployable\" config has 2.7% coverage on OH — not deployable.\n- W7: No online/intervention evaluation.\n\n**R1's Missing Experiments:**\n- Gold-set probe evaluation on OH windows\n- Larger gold set with higher IAA\n- Third agent or non-SE domain\n- Calibration analysis\n- Window stride/overlap sensitivity\n- Cost-benefit analysis of full pipeline vs direct annotation\n\n**R1's Critical Questions:**\n- Feature overlap ablation shows LF-overlapping features alone exceed full model cross-agent. How is this \"detecting true stagnation\"?\n- Human ceiling given kappa=0.39?\n- Why no probe on full gold set?\n- Nature of the \"version mismatch\" bug?\n- What happens to 97.3% of OH windows where 2-LF abstains?\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018ksKZdpf2DRA5RSyL5vqRn","session_id":"5d5323cd-d040-44cc-ba70-9f4e536cb20e","uuid":"3addadad-3d56-4495-8615-d8dfb9c2f076","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:40:56.176Z"}
